@echo off
rem ---------------------------------------------------------------------
rem DO NOT EDIT THIS FILE WHILE IT IS RUNNING. NOT EVEN A COMMENT.
rem
rem cmd.exe reads a batch file INCREMENTALLY, BY BYTE OFFSET, as it executes
rem it. Changing the file's length mid-run moves everything after the cursor,
rem and execution resumes at an offset that no longer means what it meant.
rem
rem That cost INFRA-VIEWER-001 a four-hour qualification that had PASSED: two
rem minutes in, a comment was reworded; four hours later, when qualify.cmd
rem returned, cmd.exe resumed at a stale offset and called it a SECOND time,
rem truncating qualification-times.txt and overwriting three of debug-ext's
rem logs. The run had already printed "every stage exited 0" and the evidence
rem for it was gone.
rem
rem EVERY LINE OF THIS FILE BEGINS WITH rem, set, call, echo, setlocal,
rem endlocal OR @echo, AND THAT IS CHECKED BEFORE THE RUN.
rem ---------------------------------------------------------------------
rem
rem P18-BALANCE-001 HEAT / ENERGY BALANCE. The exact invocation, recorded so the
rem run is reproducible rather than described.
rem
rem qualify.cmd is byte-identical to the one P16-SIZE-001 settled on and every
rem milestone since has used, FORTY-THREE in a row counting this one.
rem
rem   qualify.cmd          git hash-object d313a64070718c44fae290ac042fe259d1a03c8b
rem   verify-harness.cmd   git hash-object 11855b8ff891093b021d1e0351761283d0eedd24
rem
rem CMAKE_BUILD_PARALLEL_LEVEL=6, carried for the reason INFRA-VIEWER-001
rem recorded: 16 logical cores let `cmake --build` run 18 compiles at once, and
rem a CLEAN build of over 600 template-heavy translation units exhausted the
rem commit charge. Capping parallelism weakens nothing. ctest stays at -j 8.
rem
rem
rem WHAT THIS MILESTONE ADDS: the global heat accounting of an accepted thermal solution -- the
rem heat applied through faces, generated in the volume, exchanged by convection (Kconv T -
rem Qconv from the qualified boundary terms), and supplied by the prescribed temperatures (the
rem constrained components of the full residual K T - Q, or C dT/dt + K T - Q for a backward-Euler
rem step), and for a transient step the energy 1^T C dT it stores over the actual step; one sign
rem (positive INTO the body), one measured scale-aware tolerance, per-step balance of an
rem EveryStep history, atomic and bound to the solution it came from. NOTHING QUALIFIED WAS
rem CHANGED.
rem
rem   NEW          include/bettercad/thermal/ThermalBalance.hpp
rem                src/thermal/ThermalBalance.cpp
rem                tests/thermal/ThermalBalanceTests.cpp
rem                tests/thermal/ThermalBalanceMappedTests.cpp
rem                tests/thermal/ThermalBalanceTestSupport.hpp        69 cases in all
rem                tests/compile_fail/ThermalBalanceMisuse.cpp        33 cases
rem                tests/architecture/CheckBalanceOwnership.cmake     5 tests with 4 fixtures
rem   MODIFIED     src/thermal/CMakeLists.txt                  + ThermalBalance.cpp
rem                tests/CMakeLists.txt, tests/compile_fail/CMakeLists.txt  1 group
rem                tests/architecture/CMakeLists.txt           5 tests
rem                tests/cli/ZeroMatchGuard.cmake              17 filters
rem
rem What IS in the repeat set, and why. unit.Thermal selects the 69 ThermalBalance
rem cases beside the earlier thermal ones; unit.Linalg, unit.Structural, refmod. and
rem cli.structural. keep the kernel's two users in the repeat, and architecture. keeps the
rem ownership gates in it. The SELECTED COUNT IS RECORDED BY THIS RUN rather than predicted
rem here.
rem
rem compile_fail is excluded from the REPEAT for the reason the previous milestones
rem recorded: each case is a real COMPILATION. The 33 thermalbalance cases run once per
rem preset in the unfiltered ctest.
rem
rem QUALIFY_REPEAT is expanded as !REPEAT! inside qualify.cmd, never %REPEAT%:
rem a %VAR% holding | ( or ) is substituted when the for-block is PARSED and
rem closes the block early, killing the run after every preset has passed.
rem
rem THIS RUN HAPPENS ON THE HASIB MACHINE, as every milestone since P17-CLI-001,
rem by the owner's decision of 2026-10-14. GCC 16.1.0 WinLibs POSIX UCRT r4,
rem the CMake 4.4.1 and Ninja it bundles, and the dependency prefix built by
rem deps/CMakeLists.txt from the same hash-verified archives: Qt 6.11.2, OCCT
rem 8.0.1, zlib 1.3.1, Netgen 6.2.2604.
rem
rem What differs from the uqhas machine, and why each is in the CACHE rather
rem than on this line:
rem   BETTERCAD_BUILD_ROOT        C:/Users/hasib/bcdev/bc-build, below
rem   BETTERCAD_DEPS_PREFIX       C:/Users/hasib/bcdev/bettercad-deps/
rem                               gnu-16-mingw-amd64 (AppData virtualisation
rem                               under the packaged desktop app)
rem   FETCHCONTENT_SOURCE_DIR_*   Catch2, nlohmann_json and Eigen from
rem                               archives verified against the SHA256 in
rem                               cmake/BetterCADDependencies.cmake, because
rem                               the bundled CMake's curl has no CA trust
rem                               anchors (carried constraint 7).
rem Each tree was configured with those three -D flags for P17-CLI-001;
rem qualify.cmd's plain `cmake --preset` reuses the cache.
setlocal
set "BETTERCAD_BUILD_ROOT=C:/Users/hasib/bcdev/bc-build"
set "CMAKE_BUILD_PARALLEL_LEVEL=6"
set "QUALIFY_PRESETS=debug-ext release-ext debug-shared-ext"
set "QUALIFY_REPEAT_PRESETS=release-ext debug-ext"
set "QUALIFY_REPEAT=architecture|unit\.Linalg|unit\.Structural|unit\.Thermal|unit\.P17Qualification|unit\.Quality|unit\.MeshDofMap|unit\.ConstraintSet|unit\.FreeEquationMap|unit\.Tet4Element|unit\.Mesh|unit\.Volume|unit\.Tet|unit\.Siz|unit\.Id|unit\.ReferenceModel|unit\.Analytic|unit\.View|refmod\.|gui\.|cli\.structural\."
call "%~dp0qualify.cmd" "%~dp0."
set "RESULT=%errorlevel%"
echo qualify.cmd exit %RESULT%
endlocal & exit /b %RESULT%
